{"id":"AJC.maintenance.build.resource-budgets.quot-presentation","title":"Quot presentation budgets","status":"pending","depends_on":[],"owner":"","inbox_refs":[],"summary":"Ten adjacent scopes in QuotScheme presentation descent remain candidates: five 2M command budgets paired with five 800k synthesis budgets. Equivalent pullback wrappers already shed similar scopes, but this target costs about 6:42 and has eleven direct consumers."}
{"id":"AJC.grquot.genericflatness","title":"Generic flatness and finite presentation","status":"done","depends_on":[],"owner":"","inbox_refs":[],"summary":"Sorry-free. Geometric generic flatness for a finite-type morphism, stability of finite presentation under pullback, and the finite-presentation functor. Modules: Picard/GenericFlatnessGeometric, Picard/PullbackFinitePresentation, Picard/FinitePresentationFunctor."}
{"id":"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.galois-action","title":"The semilinear Galois action on a picEt-representing scheme: FREE from the representation, or the campaign's extra deliverable","status":"done","depends_on":[],"owner":"","inbox_refs":[],"summary":""}
{"id":"AJC.picrep.etale-rep.quotient-hom","title":"The GOAL's Hom-side: IsGaloisQuotient clause 3 as an Equiv, composed with the k'-representation","status":"done","depends_on":[],"owner":"","inbox_refs":[],"summary":"DONE. Commit 3683eb65bf lands quotientHomEquiv_uniform: a single Nonempty of the natural family of Hom Equivs across every test, the form required by RepresentableBy consumers. It uses only Field K, Field L, and Algebra K L; no finite-dimensionality or Galois hypothesis. This closes the Hom-side descent brick, not PicEt representability or the fgaPicardRepresentability seam. The per-test quotientHomEquiv remains as a lower-level theorem."}
{"id":"AJCR.review-plan","title":"August 2026 AJCR-first rank-one recovery plan","status":"active","depends_on":[],"owner":"","inbox_refs":[],"summary":"Binding route from the mathematician review: Div^g represented -> DivRankOneOpen -> rankOneAbelIso -> PicRankOneOpen -> translated cover over a separably closed field -> pic0_sepClosed_representableBy -> shared finite-Galois descent -> pic0_representableBy -> JacobianData. High-degree Abel quotient work is fallback infrastructure only. Endpoint credit requires root reachability, an immediate consumer, a kernel build, an axiom audit, and deletion or specialization of the obsolete path."}
{"id":"AJCR.review-plan.p3-rank-one-loci","title":"Phase 3: one public rank-one Picard and divisor locus","status":"blocked","depends_on":["AJCR.review-plan.p4-family-producer"],"owner":"ajcr-review-rank-one-openness","inbox_refs":[],"summary":"Define PicRankOneOpen by R^1-vanishing, rank-one locally free pushforward, and base-change compatibility; define DivRankOneOpen from the universal divisor on Div^g; prove openness and arbitrary base change; make chartLocus/H0Rank/H1 predicates implementation lemmas or equivalences. Acceptance: one public good-locus API consumed by the canonical inverse task. Blocked on AJCR.review-plan.p4-family-producer."}
{"id":"AJCR.review-plan.p4-rank-one-iso","title":"Phase 4: canonical family-level rank-one Abel isomorphism","status":"blocked","depends_on":[],"owner":"ajcr-review-family-producer","inbox_refs":[],"summary":"Construct divisorOfRankOne from the evaluation map f^* f_* L -> L without choosing a generator; prove its zero scheme is finite locally free of degree g, base-change compatible, and Picard-equivalent up to pullback. Prove both inverse laws, rankOneAbelIso, and rankOneAbel_isOpenImmersion on arbitrary test schemes; delete generator-selection, fieldwise-only, and source/test coupling workarounds no longer consumed. Integrate the shared family-level producer as the first Phase-4 blocker owner."}
{"id":"AJCR.review-plan.p4-family-producer","title":"Phase 4A: arbitrary-affine rank-one presentation/base-change producer","status":"active","depends_on":[],"owner":"ajcr-review-family-producer","inbox_refs":[],"summary":"Reviewer supervision note 2026-08-07 identifies this as the single shared Phase-3/5 structural blocker. Acceptance contract: produce arbitrary-affine PicRankOneNativePresentation / FibrePresented data for the actual family; prove cartesian pushforward/base-change IsIso for every public-locus pullback; tie H1=0, H0 finite-projective rank one, and the native presentation to the same object coherently under affine pullback; construct the arbitrary-test divisor with base-change compatibility; consume it immediately in PicRankOneOpen / DivRankOneOpen and rankOneAbelIso; run narrow critical-path build, axiom audit, and root/index the result. Do not credit fieldwise substitutes, vacuous wrappers, or unrelated carriers."}
{"id":"AJCR.review-plan.p5-sepclosed-cover","title":"Phase 5: translated rank-one cover over a separably closed field","status":"blocked","depends_on":["AJCR.review-plan.p4-family-producer"],"owner":"ajcr-review-sepclosed-cover","inbox_refs":[],"summary":"The general per-K/per-lambda producer and its Pic0 specialization are complete: finite-separable splitting, the positive FLV twist, actual rational-point-image support, residue degree one, baseSubtraction, and IsSplitWitness now additionally expose translator degree genus and finite-support/residue-one/exact descended-class compatibility for the same subtraction divisor. Commit 7decac68b5 roots these APIs in Pic0CriticalPath and 42b53cf822 registers their lean_ok graph nodes. The remaining blocker is a production arbitrary-affine presentation family: cartesian pushforward/base-change control plus tied H0/H1/rank data and coherent native presentations on every affine pullback, sufficient to feed PicRankOneOpen/FibrePresented. The native line-bundle piece already exists; no fieldwise substitute, high-degree Abel quotient, or Galois descent route is used. Blocked on AJCR.review-plan.p4-family-producer."}
{"id":"AJCR.review-plan.p8-jacobian","title":"Phase 8: construct JacobianData from the pinned Pic^0 representation","status":"pending","depends_on":["AJCR.review-plan.p7-galois-descent"],"owner":"","inbox_refs":[],"summary":"Use the same pic0_representableBy datum for the group object, identity component, universal element, finite type/properness/smoothness/dimension g, Abel-Jacobi map, Albanese universal property, base-change isomorphism, and cocycle coherence. Complete jacobianData, audit protected challenge declarations, and require narrow/full builds with no project-specific axioms or sorryAx."}
